6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least 10 years and valid for as long as you offer
spare parts or customer service for that product, to give anyone who
possesses the product a copy of the Corresponding Source on a
durable physical medium usually used for software distribution, for
a price no more than your reasonable cost of performing this
conveyance; or

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer to provide the Corresponding Source from a network
server at no charge, for a duration that is no less than the duration
of the offer to the object code, and as long as anyone is willing
to obtain it; or

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium usually used for
software distribution; or

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(granted by the copyright holder), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source at no charge through a network server. The
Corresponding Source must be available for a duration that is no less
than the duration of the offer for the object code, and at least
as long as copies of the object code are being distributed; or

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source is being
offered to the general public for no charge under the terms of this
License.

A separable portion of the object code whose source code is excluded
from the Corresponding Source as a System Library need not be included
in the Corresponding Source.

