    GNU Affero General Public License for more details.

    You should have received a copy of the GNU Affero General Public License
    along with this program. If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

Also add information on how to contact you by electronic and paper mail.

If your software can interact with users remotely through a computer
network, you should also make sure that it provides a way for users to
get its source code. For example, if your software is a web application,
its interface should display a link to the source code. The GNU Affero
General Public License requires the operator of the network server to
provide the source code of the modified version running there to the
users of that server. Therefore, if you modify the Program, you must
ensure that the modified version provides this functionality.

